  "metadata": {
    "name": "Counterexample — an edge with no condition",
    "description": "Violates ONLY the \"edge_with_condition\" rule: the topology is sound, but the single edge has an empty condicao. A transition with no label is a path the executor does not know when to take — and what the rule prevents is precisely a node choosing its path freely at runtime (principle 2 of the README). This counterexample is also invalid against the JSON Schema (condicao has minLength 1): the rule exists separately because the synthesizer assembles a graph in memory, before any serialization.",
    "schema_version": "1.0.0",
    "created_at": "2026-08-14",
    "source": "the specification's counterexample"
  },
